---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Our History" description="Since 1992, Burnham Nationwide has redefined permit expediting and code consulting. Explore more than 30 years of iconic projects and nationwide growth." nav="about">
  <div class="page-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <ol class="crumbs"><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li>About</li><li>History</li></ol>
      <nav aria-label="About Burnham"><a href="/about/why-burnham/">Why Burnham</a><a href="/about/team/">Team</a><a href="/about/history/" aria-current="page">History</a><a href="/about/testimonials/">Testimonials</a><a href="/about/careers/">Careers</a><a href="/diversity-inclusion/">Diversity</a><a href="/about/faq/">FAQ</a></nav>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2 grid--center">
      <div class="stack">
        <div class="eyebrow">History</div>
        <h1 class="h-display">A legacy of providing special experiences.</h1>
        <p class="lede">In 1992, when gas cost around a dollar a gallon, the Sears Tower was the world’s tallest building and the Chicago Bulls were winning their second consecutive NBA title, founding partners Mike Gaynor and Carson Kyhl came together with a shared vision: a special experience for maintaining municipal compliance in the construction industry.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="stack stack--sm" style="margin: 0;">
        <div class="media"><img src="/assets/img/about/founders.jpg" alt="Founders Mike Gaynor and Carson Kyhl in Burnham polo shirts, early 1990s" width="1600" height="1273"></div>
        <figcaption class="small">Mike Gaynor (left) and Carson Kyhl (right).</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--deep section--tight" aria-label="Milestones at a glance">
    <div class="wrap stats">
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat__value">1992</div><div class="stat__label">founded in Chicago</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat__value">1998</div><div class="stat__label">first office outside Chicago, in New York</div></div>
      <div class="stat"><div class="stat__value">30</div><div class="stat__label">years in business, celebrated in 2022</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid grid--2">
      <div class="stack history-intro">
        <div class="eyebrow">Our history</div>
        <h2 class="h-section">From one Chicago office to a national practice.</h2>
        <p class="lede">Three decades of new offices, new services and some of the country’s most recognizable buildings.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="timeline">
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">1992</div><p class="timeline__body">Burnham opens in Chicago, setting out to redefine the process of securing permit approvals.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">1995</div><p class="timeline__body">Burnham moves into a larger space to serve a growing client roster.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">1997</div><p class="timeline__body">A new division adds code consulting and architectural support services.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">1998</div><div class="timeline__title">Burnham takes on New York</div><p class="timeline__body">The New York office opens, supporting an inaugural client.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">2000</div><p class="timeline__body">The firm becomes BurnhamOnline.com, rebrands with a new look and relocates to The Burnham Center.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">2005</div><p class="timeline__body">The Denver office opens, raising the bar for permit expediting and building code compliance in the Mile High City.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">2008</div><p class="timeline__body">Burnham pulls the permits for the name change from the Sears Tower to the Willis Tower.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">2009</div><p class="timeline__body">Burnham Energy opens in San Jose, helping commercial and utility-scale developers through the solar planning, submission and approval process.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">2012</div><p class="timeline__body">The Los Angeles office opens to serve existing clients and new opportunities.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">2013</div><p class="timeline__body">Burnham launches the <a class="link" href="/our-technology/burnham-eye/">BurnhamEYE™</a> app, streamlining solar system verifications and letting field staff compile and update information in real time.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">2014</div><div class="timeline__title">Setting records</div><p class="timeline__body">Burnham and the Wilshire Grand Center project team enter the Guinness World Records with the largest continuous mat pour in history: more than 21,240 cubic yards of concrete.</p><p class="timeline__body"><a class="link" href="/portfolio/wilshire-grand-center/">See the project</a></p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">2015</div><p class="timeline__body">The San Francisco office opens to serve clients and satellites across Northern California. The same year, Walgreens rolls out Little Clinic facilities with help from Burnham.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">2016</div><div class="timeline__title">A recipe for success</div><p class="timeline__body">When Starbucks begins selling warm food, Burnham pulls permits nationwide to support the rollout.</p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">2017</div><p class="timeline__body">Burnham pulls the permits for Chicago’s Wanda Vista Tower, set to become the city’s third-tallest building and the tallest structure in the world designed by a woman.</p><p class="timeline__body"><a class="link" href="/portfolio/vista/">See the project</a></p></li>
        <li class="timeline__item"><div class="timeline__year">2022</div><p class="timeline__body">Burnham turns 30.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--flush-top">
    <div class="wrap cta-block">
      <div class="stack stack--sm">
        <h2>Your project could be next.</h2>
        <p>Tell us about it, and a project manager will map the path to approval.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Contact Burnham Nationwide</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
